concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-1-sec-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 After subsection 19AL(2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-4 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (2A) If the Attorney-General does not, under paragraph (2)(b), reconsider the making of a parole order for a person and either make, or refuse to make, such an order before the end of the 12 month period referred to in that paragraph, the Attorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the end of that period, reconsider and either make, or refuse to make, a parole order for the person. Contents of parole order" ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (2A) If the Attorney-General does not, under paragraph (2)(b), reconsider the making of a parole order for a person and either make, or refuse to make, such an order before the end of the 12 month period referred to in that paragraph, the Attorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the end of that period, reconsider and either make, or refuse to make, a parole order for the person. Contents of parole order"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7a8444fb9f3dfbb18340612a847ad777e7009abb9f798606c5e2effcbfac6645" ;
    cof:pageNumber "7"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Attorney-General must reconsider and make a parole order for a person if not done within 12 months." ;
