concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 Section 300.2 of the Criminal Code (definition of border"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-1 ;
    values:originalText "controlled drug) Repeal the definition, substitute: border controlled drug:  (a) means a substance that is a border controlled drug within the meaning of subsection 301.4(1); and  (b) to avoid doubt, includes a substance that is, under subsection 301.4(2), (3) or 301.13(1A), taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled drug only in relation to particular offences against this Part or particular elements of those offences." ;
    skos:definition "controlled drug) Repeal the definition, substitute: border controlled drug:  (a) means a substance that is a border controlled drug within the meaning of subsection 301.4(1); and  (b) to avoid doubt, includes a substance that is, under subsection 301.4(2), (3) or 301.13(1A), taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled drug only in relation to particular offences against this Part or particular elements of those offences."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "08d9a2a68e07d7eaa237d61439e187b669a28c710d6e5a049fd9b035c9038542" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definition of border controlled drug" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
