concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-12 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12 After subsection 301.6(1) of the Criminal Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-12 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (1A) However:  (a) the regulations may provide that a listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to particular offences against this Part, or particular elements of those offences; and  (b) if the regulations so provide, then the listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to those offences or elements.  (1B) To avoid doubt, if a listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to particular offences against this Part, or particular elements of those offences, then a salt, ester or immediate precursor of the listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to those offences or elements.  Schedule 2  Border controlled drugs, plants and precursors  Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 2) Act 2023 No. 98, 2023  Definition of immediate precursor" ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (1A) However:  (a) the regulations may provide that a listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to particular offences against this Part, or particular elements of those offences; and  (b) if the regulations so provide, then the listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to those offences or elements.  (1B) To avoid doubt, if a listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to particular offences against this Part, or particular elements of those offences, then a salt, ester or immediate precursor of the listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in relation to those offences or elements.  Schedule 2  Border controlled drugs, plants and precursors  Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 2) Act 2023 No. 98, 2023  Definition of immediate precursor"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-12-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-12-ss-1b ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
