concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Subsection 112A(3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (3) Subsection (4) applies if a substance is a border controlled precursor because of a determination made under section 301.14 of the Criminal Code (which deals with emergency Ministerial determinations of serious drug precursors). Note: Border controlled precursor has the same meaning as in Part 9.1 of the Criminal Code (see subsection 4(1) of this Act). In that Part, that term includes substances that are, under section 301.14 of the Criminal Code, taken, for the purposes of the Part, to be border controlled precursors only in relation to particular offences against the Part, or particular elements of those offences. Defence Force Discipline Act 1982" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (3) Subsection (4) applies if a substance is a border controlled precursor because of a determination made under section 301.14 of the Criminal Code (which deals with emergency Ministerial determinations of serious drug precursors). Note: Border controlled precursor has the same meaning as in Part 9.1 of the Criminal Code (see subsection 4(1) of this Act). In that Part, that term includes substances that are, under section 301.14 of the Criminal Code, taken, for the purposes of the Part, to be border controlled precursors only in relation to particular offences against the Part, or particular elements of those offences. Defence Force Discipline Act 1982"@en ;
